<Layout title="About me">
  <p>
    CTO with a PhD in Operations Research who still writes solvers, wins federal grants, and ships
    products to Air Force bases. I am co-founder and CTO at{' '}
    <a href="https://www.opslab.com">OpsLab</a>, where I lead engineering and research on
    AI-powered scheduling and operations software for military warfighters. Deep expertise in
    large-scale optimization, LLM-powered workflows, and autonomous systems. Track record of turning
    hard operational problems into deployed software that measurably changes how people work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Based in Chandler, AZ. Reach me at{' '}
    <a href="mailto:sujeevraja26@gmail.com">sujeevraja26@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h1 class="f4 lh-title">Background</h1>
  <p>
    After completing a PhD at Texas A&M and a post-doctoral fellowship at UC Berkeley, I spent 8
    years at Sabre Airline Solutions building and leading production optimization solvers for
    real-time crew and aircraft schedule recovery — systems deployed by major international airlines.
    In 2022 I co-founded OpsLab, where we have won $800K in federal SBIR funding, deployed our
    scheduling platform across 8 USAF squadrons (achieving a 94% reduction in schedule creation
    time), and built LLM-based workflow tooling on top of our optimization core.
  </p>

